  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certifies that on 05th June 2006, the erection of a single storey side and rear extension and raised decking, as shown on drawing number 02/06-SC/C, received 05th June 2006, is less than 15% of the entire gross floor area of the existing dwelling, so therefore was lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\nFollowing the proposed erection of a single storey side (1.85m wide, 7.0m deep & 3.8m high) and rear extension (4.1m wide, 1.8m deep & 3.8m high) and raised decking, the resulting building would fall within the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class A of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995.\r\n"
